nearly a dozen young men are charged  with hazing in the death of a Louisiana  State University freshman Maxwell  groover died last month after becoming  highly intoxicated at a fraternity  pledge event 10 current and former LSU  students are accused of forcing forcing  this 18 year old to heavily drink  groover is at least a second student to  die this year after a hazing incident  involving alcohol in February you may  remember Penn State student Timothy  Piazza died Omar Villafranca is on LSU's  campus in Baton Rouge  Omar good morning good morning all 10  suspects were members of the Phi Delta  Theta fraternity here at LSU but the  National Organization has since  terminated their membership now  witnesses say groover was targeted  because he was often late to events and  they forced him to drink because he had  trouble reciting the Greek alphabet  during pledging it took less than 5  hours for all 10 current and former LSU  students to surrender to campus police  on Wednesday the men were arrested and  brought to the local prison all are  charged with one misdemeanor count of  hazing 19-year old Matthew nock Han is  also charged with a felony count of  negligent homicide  according to the affidavit he was the  most aggressive during the alleged  hazing incident his bail was set at  $10,000 nine of the suspects were  released on bond in less than 24 hours I  don't think he's gonna be pleading  guilty at this point Franz Beauregard is  an attorney for Shawn Penniston I don't  know what happened in that fraternity  house I have my clients version of the  story I'm looking forward to seeing  everyone else's version of the story  we're gonna do it in a court of law an  arrest warrant shows pledges received a  text message on September 13th ordering  them to Bible study at 10 p.m. at the  chapter house once their pledges were  quizzed about the fraternities history  if they answered a question incorrectly  they were forced to drink 190-proof  alcohol around midnight  witnesses say groover was highly  intoxicated and left on a couch nine  hours later he was found with a weak  pulse fraternity members took him to the  hospital where he was pronounced dead an  autopsy revealed groovers blood-alcohol  level will  point four nine five percent at the time  of his death more than six times the  legal driving limit and nearly two times  what's considered to be a  life-threatening level of alcohol  Justin Franklin shared a suite with  Gruber in a dorm on campus if you're  supposed to be a club full of friends  and people who have life lasting  relationships what his life have to end  so early if convicted of hazing the  suspects could get 30 days in jail and  also expelled from LSU now if convicted  nach Han could get five years in prison  for that negligent homicide charge the  district attorney does plan to take over  in the investigation and says more  charges could be filed Charlie thanks  Omar
 

